## builtins_table.src -- every builtin of the language, in one table: the single source of truth.
##
## One row per name: `name arity effect lists def doc reg`.
##   arity   the argument count name_flow holds a call to (nf_ar0..nf_ar3, nf_builtin_arity), or - when the name is
##           only produced by the compiler itself (sugar, internal routines), which supplies the arguments
##   effect  the effect a call adds (06b_phase3 kprim_eff0 / kprim_eff_rt and lcaas cs_kprim_eff): pure, io, fs, net,
##           sys, time, alloc, rand, prob, llm, wasm, ffi, fail, panic, async
##   lists   the name_flow predicates that hold the name, comma-separated, or -: rt (nf_rtbase), sys (lis_sys_call:
##           its label is in the runtime_sys_tail text), tier (lis_tier_call), mem (lis_mem_call), bv1 / bv2
##           (lis_bv1_call / lis_bv2_call), ct (lis_ct_call), int (nf_internal: a runtime routine no program calls)
##   def     where its code comes from: core (a label of runtime_core.lume), lume (a function of rt/*.src, compiled
##           into runtime_lume.lume by gen_runtime), cg (a label 05_codegen.src emits), inline (lowered in place by
##           05_codegen.src), - (an effect-only name: sugar or a library function the effect checker knows)
##   doc     ref when docs/LUME_REFERENCE_EN.md and _PT_BR.md show it as NAME(...), else -
##   reg     yes when compiler/stage1/builtins_regress_ok.src calls it, skip when it is documented but cannot run
##           inside a test process, no otherwise
##
## Adding a builtin: add its row here, run the generator (`printf '@root %s\n@mode gen\n' "$PWD" | build/bin/builtins_gate`
## after `lume build tests/harness/builtins_gate.src -o build/bin/builtins_gate`), which rewrites the name_flow,
## 06b_phase3 and lcaas lists from this table, then define it in the runtime, document it and call it in
## builtins_regress_ok.src until the gate (`@mode check`, run by bootstrap/lume0/tests/run.sh) reports nothing.
fn builtins_table() = """
# name                         ar   effect  lists        def     doc  reg
__lume_arc_new                 -    alloc   tier         cg      -    no
__lume_arena_alloc             2    alloc   mem          lume    -    no
__lume_arena_destroy           1    pure    mem          lume    -    no
__lume_arena_freeze            -    alloc   mem          lume    -    no
__lume_arena_frozen            -    alloc   mem          lume    -    no
__lume_arena_new               1    alloc   mem          lume    -    no
